  ],
  reason: "gunbc#12886. Native recursion over a VALUE's depth (which no call limit counts) killed the interpreter with rc=134 and no location (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode recursion_over_value_depth_uncounted_by_the_call_limit). Added: value_depth_guarded, the one guard every recursive walker over a Value runs under; detach_owned_children, the worklist behind an iterative Drop; the JSON-depth refusal (serde_json_read_depth_limit, claim_json_nesting, JsonNestingClaim, json_container_depth, and the fixture codec's fixture_nesting and value_to_fixture_json_shape with the FixtureError variant); and the deep-value test modules. Changed: every walker now guarded, and Value's derive (Debug is hand-written under the guard). UNCITABLE, also added or changed: impl Drop for Value, impl fmt::Debug for Value, impl Drop for JsonNestingClaim, impl PartialEq for Value (eq), impl fmt::Display for Value (fmt), impl fmt::Display for FixtureError (fmt), the thread_local JSON_ENCODE_NESTING, and the census unguarded_recursive_value_walkers in src/v1/stage0/build.rs, which no rust_source_namespace_rows prefix claims. The value representation and its traversals are the seed interpreter's host data structure, so no .dag authority can host the repair.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete with the seed interpreter itself: when claims are evaluated on the emitted path rather than by v1_interpreter (the v1-interpreter-quarantine then v1-interpreter-delete lanes), this Rust has no evaluator left to correct and goes with the file. It has no earlier trigger, because the interpreter's evaluation semantics have no .dag authority that an earlier move could migrate into. Its own next rung is recorded on the failure-mode row: one generic iterative Value traversal through which every walker is expressed.",
  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs, recorded_fixture.rs, cli_run.rs, coproduct_reflection.rs, build.rs",
}

