  reason: "gunbc#12886, the mechanical half. Implementing Drop on Value makes moving a field out of a Value a compile error (E0509), so every site that destructured an owned Value by move now binds by reference -- the compiler's own `ref` suggestion applied at each site, plus three hand fixes. No behaviour changes at these sites; they are listed because the admission policy covers every modified hand item, and an adaptation forced by another change is still a modification. UNCITABLE, also changed the same way: impl ScopedRunObservation (timing_receipt) and impl UnimportedBareProviderRosterReading (identity). ALREADY JUSTIFIED BY THEIR OWN ROWS, and so not repeated here because the roster cites each declaration once: portable_value_eq, portable_value_from_ctx_at, portable_value_size_bytes, admit_modeled_realization, file_result_of_observation, file_effect_trace_tests (render, file_mode_octal_agrees_with_the_posix_authority_over_the_admitted_range), required_regen_host (admit_candidate_generation_from_model, admit_stage_execution_from_model, convergence_plan_from_model, regen_generation_role_population, regen_round_cost_tests live_module_mirrors_have_owners_and_removed_shell_owner_refuses) and data_initializer_identity with_authored_string_literals -- each also carries this change's guard or ref-binding edit.",
